menu "A2DP Example Configuration"
    config EXAMPLE_LOCAL_DEVICE_NAME
        string "Local Device Name"
        default "ESP_SPEAKER"
        help
            Use this option to set local device name.

    config EXAMPLE_A2DP_SINK_USE_EXTERNAL_CODEC
        bool "Use External Codec Instead of Internal"
        default n
        select BT_A2DP_USE_EXTERNAL_CODEC
        help
            If enable, Bluedroid stack will not decode A2DP audio data, user need to decode it in application layer.

endmenu

menu "Bridge status LEDs"
    config BRIDGE_LED_CONNECTED_GPIO
        int "Connected LED GPIO (-1 to disable)"
        range -1 33
        default 32
        help
            Solid on while a phone is connected over A2DP, off otherwise.

            Wire the LED from the pin through a resistor (330 ohm is fine) to
            ground; the pin drives it high. Anything above GPIO 33 cannot be
            used -- 34-39 on a classic ESP32 are input-only.

            GPIO 13, 14, 15 and 25 belong to the SPI link to the hub and must
            not be used here.

    config BRIDGE_LED_STREAMING_GPIO
        int "Streaming LED GPIO (-1 to disable)"
        range -1 33
        default 33
        help
            Blinks at 0.5 Hz while A2DP audio packets are arriving, dark
            when the phone is paused or the stream has stopped. It follows the
            packets themselves, not the reported stream state, so a stalled
            stream goes dark even if the phone still calls itself playing.

endmenu
